>
> Altars to Molach would have a 100% chance of cursing
> your items.

I'd say do what you're suggesting for cross-aligned altars for Moloch's
altars instead, and forget about having Moloch's altars auto-cursing
objects.

But even that could be considered way too powerful. After all, it would
make those altars actually quite useful: finally, a way to reliably
produce unholy water and cursed scrolls of genocide and so on.

Note that the lack of a reliable way of cursing objects is a major problem
in NetHack, and you're solving that problem.

> If your god is mad at you, or your alignment is lacking,
> then s/he/it would curse your items as well.

Again, this would in some way make it *useful* to have an angry god...

> Moral: Stay in your god's good graces

You should be doing that anyway. Perhaps a conduct could be made of this:
"You were always in good grace with your god". Quite difficult to keep, I
would say, especially since there is no simple way to check this (you'd
have to constantly use a stethoscope on yourself to be certain).

> Perhaps priests should lose their ability to auto
> ID if their alignment is too low, or their god is
> angry.

I like this idea. Why not extrapolate this to all other classes (special
class abilities don't work when your god is angry?). This of course
presumes that your god has something to do with your class, which figures,
since every class gets its own gods.

